
.claude/
*.ez
/_build/
/cover/
/deps/
/doc/
/tmp/
# Also ignore archive artifacts (built via "mix archive.build").
# claude-managed worktrees for approved agent work
# If the VM crashes, it generates a dump, let's ignore it too.
# If you run "mix test --cover", coverage assets end up here.
# Ignore package tarball (built via "mix hex.build").
# Temporary files, for example, from tests.
# The activity feed is runtime state, not source.
# The demo database is runtime state, not source.
# The directory Mix downloads your dependencies sources to.
# The directory Mix will write compiled artifacts to.
# Where third-party dependencies like ExDoc output generated docs.
custode-*.tar
custode.db*
dev-workspace/journal.md
dev-workspace/TODO.md
erl_crash.dump
# Dialyzer PLTs (built artifacts, cached in CI, never source).
/priv/plts/
feed.jsonl
workspace/inbox/
workspace/journal.md
workspace/TODO.md
workspaces/*/inbox/
workspaces/*/journal.md
workspaces/*/TODO.md

# Workspace runtime data: journal.md/TODO.md are regenerable views of db
# records (design/002) and inbox notes are runtime messages -- none of it is
# source. Tracked copies also kept getting swept into unrelated commits by
# operator add -A (#117, #144); untracked, that class is gone.
workspace/
workspaces/
dev-workspace/

# live roster written by the runtime in dev-loop mode; never commit
/routines.toml
